/*
 * Declares the NamedValue class.
 *
 * NamedValue represents a named argument in a function call. A named argument
 * assigns a specific value to a specific parameter by name rather than by
 * positional order.
 *
 * Example:
 *
 *     foo(7, a -> 12)
 *
 * Here, the argument `a -> 12` binds the value `12` to the parameter named `a`,
 * regardless of its position in the function’s parameter list.
 *
 * <hr>
 * 
 * @Package: ymirc        
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::generator::value::operator::named
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/generator/value/operator/named.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created (YYYY-MM-DD): 2021-11-20
 * @Copyright (C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
 * @License
 *   ```text
